        "created_at": "2026-08-30T21:34:26.347Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Thanks for the figures.<br>\nI’m confused though - if I assume that <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/ky_rah\">@Ky_rah</a> has already used a referral link (for the 1M SP) then the character would have a value of around 700M ISK based on the total SP being roughly 1.5M right now.</p>\n<p>If no referral link has been used yet (unlikely, I’m thinking) then the character would have a value of around 3x0.7M = 2.1M ISK (as QSNA suggests), and yet the buy-out price for the character is 4B ISK, so I’m clearly missing something pretty important.<br>\n(And of course I’m not understanding where that 1.5B ISK saving is to be had.)</p>",
